{
  "apiVersion": 2,
  "name": "Mirally development worker pools",
  "description": "Mirally adaptation of the dsh-auto-workflow development example: workflow-owned requirements, one retained detached worktree per item, 3+3 review pools, human merge gate and local-only integration into integration/auto-workflow. Start one producer packet explicitly at mine-gate; user arrivals enqueue dispatch.",
  "entry": "dispatch",
  "concurrency": 6,
  "historyLimit": 100,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "dispatch",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Admit queued items",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRoot": "$input.dataRoot",
        "batchSize": 3
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs claim",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "work-fanout",
      "type": "fanout",
      "title": "Queue work packets",
      "config": {
        "items": "$prev.items",
        "target": "route",
        "detached": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mine-gate",
      "type": "gate",
      "title": "Mining switch",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRoot": "$input.dataRoot"
      },
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 60000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "queue-check",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Check implementation backlog",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRoot": "$input.dataRoot",
        "maxPending": 3
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs queue-check",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seed-batch",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Claim seed batch",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRoot": "$input.dataRoot",
        "batchSize": 3
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs seed-batch",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seed-fanout",
      "type": "fanout",
      "title": "Queue mining packets",
      "config": {
        "items": "$prev.items",
        "target": "miner",
        "detached": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "producer-dispatch",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Admit priority queue",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRoot": "$input.dataRoot",
        "batchSize": 3
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs claim",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "producer-work",
      "type": "fanout",
      "title": "Queue found work",
      "config": {
        "items": "$prev.items",
        "target": "route",
        "detached": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "miner",
      "type": "agent",
      "title": "Mine one seed",
      "role": "analyst",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "cwd": "$input.cwd",
        "outcomes": [
          "proposal",
          "idle"
        ],
        "prompt": "Mine one seed for genuinely useful, varied work. Read the seed JSON at input.dataRef, the requirement queue under input.dataRoot/requirements, recent commits, tests, docs and relevant source in cwd. First generate 3-5 candidate directions, covering correctness/regression, reliability/error handling, performance, UX/accessibility, test gaps/observability, security/data safety and maintainability/tooling. For each candidate state evidence, impact, risk and the smallest verifiable acceptance. Discard duplicates of existing requirements, weak or evidence-free ideas, pure style preferences and anything not independently shippable. Then choose the single highest-value concrete change. Seeds with origin=baseline are discovery directions, not proof: return idle if the repository does not support a concrete proposal. Do not invent another seed or requirement id. Do not edit the repository or business store and do not invoke approval services. Risk is your assessment: low (local reversible), mid (cross-module/uncertain), high (security/destructive/external). Return outcome proposal with output {proposal:{title,description,risk,priority:1..9,tags:[]}}, or outcome idle with output {proposal:null}. The record command derives the same stable requirement id from this seed. No default task deadline is set.\n\nProject adaptation (Mirally): the repository is a Python product (mirally/) with an in-repo DeepSeek Harness kernel (kernel/dsh/), tests (tests/) and docs (docs/). Read AGENTS.md before proposing. Prefer a scoped change with a concrete verification path; avoid proposals that require remote services, credentials, deployment or GUI-only verification that cannot be checked from the worktree."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "record-proposal",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Persist mined item",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "seedId": "$input.seedId",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "proposal": "$prev.proposal"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs record-proposal",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "route",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Apply risk policy",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs route",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "requirement-human",
      "type": "human",
      "title": "Requirement pending",
      "config": {
        "title": "Approve mid/high risk requirement or reject with feedback",
        "outcomes": [
          "approve",
          "reject"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "approve-requirement",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Record approval",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "expectedRevision": "$nodes.route.output.revision",
        "decision": "approve",
        "note": "$prev.note",
        "actor": "$prev.actor"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs requirement-decision",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "reject-requirement",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Record feedback",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "expectedRevision": "$nodes.route.output.revision",
        "decision": "reject",
        "note": "$prev.note",
        "actor": "$prev.actor"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs requirement-decision",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "analyst-revise",
      "type": "agent",
      "title": "Revise same requirement",
      "role": "analyst",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "cwd": "$input.cwd",
        "outcomes": [
          "complete"
        ],
        "prompt": "Read input.dataRef, especially current revision and human requirement feedback. Revise this SAME requirement; never create a new id and never edit store files directly. Return output {proposal:{expectedRevision:<current revision>,title,description,risk:low|mid|high,tags:[]}}. Explain intended behavior in description and honor rejection feedback. The command persists revision+1 on the original id and retains its worktree."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "revise-proposal",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Persist same-id revision",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "proposal": "$prev.proposal"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs revise-proposal",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "prepare",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Prepare retained worktree",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs prepare",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "begin-engineering",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Admit one engineering epoch",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs begin-engineering",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "engineer",
      "type": "agent",
      "title": "Engineers 0–3",
      "role": "engineer",
      "concurrency": 3,
      "config": {
        "cwd": "$input.cwd",
        "outcomes": [
          "complete"
        ],
        "prompt": "Work ONLY in input.cwd (the retained per-requirement Git worktree). Read input.dataRef for the stable requirement, current revision, previous immutable implementation/reviews and human feedback. Implement and run the repository's actual verification. Commit the implementation locally in this worktree so HEAD is clean. Never merge, push, delete worktrees, change base-branch checkout, edit business JSON, spawn agents, or call approval services. Return output {summary:<non-empty string describing concise changes>,verification:<non-empty string containing actual commands and results, NOT an array or object>}. Snapshot command will pin commit/tree and requirement revision; false success will fail downstream. No default task deadline.\n\nProject adaptation (Mirally): read AGENTS.md at the repository root and follow it. This worktree has no .venv: resolve the primary checkout by running `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and taking its parent directory, then use `<parent>/.venv/Scripts/python.exe`. Run targeted tests for the modules you touch, for example `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m unittest tests.<module> -v`; the full `-m unittest discover -s tests` suite includes optional UFO reference tests and is not the required gate, so do not treat that wholesale failure as a regression and never weaken or delete tests to pass. For documentation changes run `.venv/Scripts/python.exe tools/check_docs_links.py` and `.venv/Scripts/python.exe tools/check_sources.py`. For user-visible changes update CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased]. Keep the change scoped to the requirement; do not touch the integration checkout, other worktrees, credentials or product data."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "snapshot",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Freeze implementation",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "expectedRevision": "$nodes.begin-engineering.output.revision",
        "engineeringEpoch": "$nodes.begin-engineering.output.engineeringEpoch",
        "summary": "$prev.summary",
        "verification": "$prev.verification"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs snapshot",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "review-input",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Pin review admission",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs review-input",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "reviewer",
      "type": "agent",
      "title": "Reviewers 0–3",
      "role": "reviewer",
      "concurrency": 3,
      "config": {
        "cwd": "$input.cwd",
        "outcomes": [
          "pass",
          "revise"
        ],
        "prompt": "You are the ONE reviewer assigned this item from a pool of three. Read input.artifactRef, the requirement JSON at input.dataRef, and pinned commit input.commit. Review ONLY that immutable artifact, run appropriate verification, and do not edit/commit the worktree or store. Return outcome pass or revise with output {decision:<same outcome>,summary:<non-empty string of findings or rationale>,verification:<non-empty string containing actual commands and results, NOT an array or object>,reviewer:<non-empty string reviewer label>}. Never approve merge or invoke external approval services. A valid negative review goes to the SAME engineer worktree/id, not model failover.\n\nProject adaptation (Mirally): read AGENTS.md. Resolve the primary checkout with `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` (parent directory) and use its `.venv/Scripts/python.exe` for targeted verification. Full `discover -s tests` includes optional UFO tests and is not the required gate; do not fail a change solely for that wholesale failure, and do not accept weakened tests. For documentation changes require `tools/check_docs_links.py` and `tools/check_sources.py`; for user-visible changes check CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased]. Apply docs/development/review-experience.md, and docs/standards/ui-guidelines.md for UI changes. Do not edit or commit anything."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "record-review",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Freeze review revision",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "artifactRef": "$nodes.review-input.output.artifactRef",
        "commit": "$nodes.review-input.output.commit",
        "decision": "$nodes.reviewer.outcome",
        "summary": "$prev.summary",
        "verification": "$prev.verification",
        "reviewer": "$prev.reviewer"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs record-review",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "merge-human",
      "type": "human",
      "title": "Human pending pool",
      "config": {
        "title": "Approve this exact reviewed artifact for local merge, request changes, or reject (retain worktree)",
        "outcomes": [
          "approve",
          "revise",
          "reject"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "approve-merge",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Record merge approval",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "artifactRef": "$nodes.record-review.output.artifactRef",
        "decision": "approve",
        "note": "$prev.note",
        "actor": "$prev.actor"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs merge-decision",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "request-changes",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Keep worktree; revise",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "artifactRef": "$nodes.record-review.output.artifactRef",
        "decision": "revise",
        "note": "$prev.note",
        "actor": "$prev.actor"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs merge-decision",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "reject-merge",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Reject; retain worktree",
      "inputs": {
        "dataRef": "$input.dataRef",
        "claimId": "$input.claimId",
        "artifactRef": "$nodes.record-review.output.artifactRef",
        "decision": "reject",
        "note": "$prev.note",
        "actor": "$prev.actor"
      },
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs merge-decision",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "integrate",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Integrate one at a time",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs integrate",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cleanup",
      "type": "command",
      "title": "Explicit cleanup policy",
      "concurrency": 1,
      "config": {
        "command": "node docs/examples/development/driver.mjs cleanup",
        "json": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-dispatch",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-queue-check",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-seed-batch",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-producer-dispatch",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-record-proposal",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-route",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-approve-requirement",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-reject-requirement",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-revise-proposal",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-prepare",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-begin-engineering",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-snapshot",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-review-input",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-record-review",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-approve-merge",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-request-changes",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-reject-merge",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-integrate",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "busy-cleanup",
      "type": "gate",
      "config": {
        "delayMs": 1000
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
